From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:08:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 257/260] [ae-patch] Keep a claude-native bridge dir for 7 days
 after its runner dies, so a relaunch can keep the transcript

The host's startup orphan sweep removed the whole claude-native bridge dir, including
the forwarder cursor and the frontier record, whenever a relaunch lagged the sweep by a
few seconds. The relaunch then found no cursor and rebuilt the transcript.

The sweep now keeps a dead-owner dir until owner.pid and whichever of
transcript_forwarder.json and ae_transcript_frontier.json exist are all older than 7
days (the window codex-native uses). A kept dir loses only the runtime files: the six a
re-prep unlinks (server.json, state.json, hooks.jsonl, observer_hook.stderr,
tool_relay.json, tmux.json) plus tool_relay.env, which holds a token. A cold launch logs
which of the cursor and the record exist, as booleans, sizes and times.

Archiving a session now asks its runner to clean up the session's resources before the
host runner is stopped, so an archived chat's bridge dir and attachment cache go at once
instead of waiting out the window.
